    description: "WHAT (as reported)\nCommands disagree on test code for boundary claims, against the 10.0.0 statement that every command agrees on what is test code.\n1. verify-claims counts a boundary claim's evidence in test code: on flaskr \"never writes to the filesystem\" reported 3 writes, 2 of them in tests; io-boundaries on the same survey shows 1. verify-claims has no test option for boundary claims (--include-non-production-sources applies to taint claims).\n2. sketch -x leaves tests out of the summary only: the survey it saves still holds the test symbols (33 on flaskr).\n3. With survey -e tests, the scip-python backend still added an edge from tests/test_db.py.\nWorkaround the reviewer found: survey . -e tests, then verify-claims --input; a path pattern does not catch tests that sit beside the code.\n\nNOT CHECKED\nWhether verify-claims' count including tests is deliberate (a test's write is a write the repository performs).\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # 12c6
